  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-fork-to-preset",
      "text": "A [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) plugin that adds a **\"Fork to preset\"** button to every conversation's header. Pick any agent preset from the roster and fork the current session into a fresh independent child session running under that preset — inheriting the parent's completed turns."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "- Click the **↴ Fork to preset** dropdown in the conversation header\n- Select a target agent preset from the roster\n- Click the button → a new session opens, mounted on the chosen preset, with the parent's completed-turn history"
    },
    {
      "section": "Distribution",
      "text": "**GitHub-only.** Not published to npm. Install by mounting the package directory with a `cordis.patch.yml` bundle declaration.\n\nRequires a platform that has the `session.fork({ agentPreset })` API (DeepSeek Harness rc.8+)."
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Link the package into the harness install",
      "text": "```bat\n:: Windows\nmklink /J \"<plugin-dir>\\node_modules\" \"<harness>\\resources\\host\\node_modules\"\n```\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "POSIX (Linux/macOS)",
      "text": "ln -s \"<harness>/resources/host/node_modules\" \"<plugin-dir>/node_modules\"\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Add the bundle to a profile",
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": { \"dsh-fork-to-preset\": \"link:<plugin-dir>\" },\n  \"dsh\": { \"profile\": { \"bundles\": [\"...\", \"dsh-fork-to-preset\"] } }\n}"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
